   {
    "id": "p_00006",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     1
    ],
    "text": "For [I5]realloc[/I5](): [S6][[A7]CX[/A7]][/S6] [IMG8] The functionality described on this reference page is aligned with the ISO&nbsp;C standard. Any\nconflict between the requirements described here and the ISO&nbsp;C standard is unintentional. This volume of POSIX.1-2024 defers\nto the ISO&nbsp;C standard. [IMG9]",
    "placeholders": {
     "I5": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "S6": {
      "open": "<sup>",
      "close": "</sup>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A7": {
      "open": "<a href=\"javascript:open_code(&#x27;CX&#x27;)\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG8": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-start.gif\" alt=\"[Option Start]\" border=\"0\">"
     },
     "IMG9": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-end.gif\" alt=\"[Option End]\" border=\"0\">"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00007",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The [I10]realloc[/I10]() function shall deallocate the old object pointed to by [I11]ptr[/I11] and return a pointer to a new object that\nhas the size specified by [I12]size[/I12]. The contents of the new object shall be the same as that of the old object prior to\ndeallocation, up to the lesser of the new and old sizes. Any bytes in the new object beyond the size of the old object have\nindeterminate values.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I10": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I11": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I12": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00008",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     5
    ],
    "text": "[S13][[A14]CX[/A14]][/S13] [IMG15] The\n[I16]reallocarray[/I16]() function shall be equivalent to the call [CODE17] except\nthat overflow in the multiplication shall be an error. [IMG18]",
    "placeholders": {
     "S13": {
      "open": "<sup>",
      "close": "</sup>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A14": {
      "open": "<a href=\"javascript:open_code(&#x27;CX&#x27;)\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG15": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-start.gif\" alt=\"[Option Start]\" border=\"0\">"
     },
     "I16": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "CODE17": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<tt>realloc(<i>ptr</i>, <i>nelem</i> * <i>elsize</i>)</tt>"
     },
     "IMG18": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-end.gif\" alt=\"[Option End]\" border=\"0\">"
     }
    },
    "context": null
