   {
    "id": "p_00009",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     7
    ],
    "text": "If [I19]ptr[/I19] is a null pointer, [I20]realloc[/I20]() [S21][[A22]CX[/A22]][/S21] [IMG23] &nbsp;or [I24]reallocarray[/I24]() [IMG25] &nbsp;shall be equivalent to [A26][I27]malloc[/I27]()[/A26] for the specified\nsize. Otherwise, if [I28]ptr[/I28] does not match a pointer earlier returned by [A29][I30]aligned_alloc[/I30]()[/A29], [A31][I32]calloc[/I32]()[/A31], [A33][I34]malloc[/I34]()[/A33], [S35][[A36]ADV[/A36]][/S35] [IMG37] &nbsp;[A38][I39]posix_memalign[/I39]()[/A38], [IMG40]\n&nbsp;[A41][I42]realloc[/I42]()[/A41],\n\n[S43][[A44]CX[/A44]][/S43] [IMG45]\n[I46]reallocarray[/I46](), or a function in POSIX.1-2024 that allocates memory as if by [A47][I48]malloc[/I48]()[/A47], [IMG49] &nbsp;or if the\nspace has been deallocated by a call to [A50][I51]free[/I51]()[/A50], [S52][[A53]CX[/A53]][/S52] [IMG54] &nbsp;[A55][I56]reallocarray[/I56]()[/A55], [IMG57]\n&nbsp;or [I58]realloc[/I58](), &nbsp;the behavior is undefined.",
