   {
    "id": "p_00010",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     9
    ],
    "text": "If [I59]size[/I59] is non-zero and memory for the new object is not allocated, the old object shall not be deallocated.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I59": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00011",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     11
    ],
    "text": "The order and contiguity of storage allocated by successive calls to [I60]realloc[/I60]() [S61][[A62]CX[/A62]][/S61] [IMG63] &nbsp;or\n[I64]reallocarray[/I64]() [IMG65] &nbsp;is unspecified. The pointer returned if\nthe allocation succeeds shall be suitably aligned so that it may be assigned to a pointer to any type of object with a fundamental\nalignment requirement and then used to access such an object in the space allocated (until the space is explicitly freed or\nreallocated). Each such allocation shall yield a pointer to an object disjoint from any other object. The pointer returned shall\npoint to the start (lowest byte address) of the allocated space. If the space cannot be allocated, a null pointer shall be\nreturned.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I60": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "S61": {
      "open": "<sup>",
      "close": "</sup>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A62": {
      "open": "<a href=\"javascript:open_code(&#x27;CX&#x27;)\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG63": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-start.gif\" alt=\"[Option Start]\" border=\"0\">"
     },
     "I64": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG65": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-end.gif\" alt=\"[Option End]\" border=\"0\">"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00012",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     13
    ],
    "text": "For purposes of determining the existence of a data race, [I66]realloc[/I66]() [S67][[A68]CX[/A68]][/S67] [IMG69] &nbsp;and\n[I70]reallocarray[/I70]() [IMG71] &nbsp;shall each behave as though it accessed\nonly memory locations accessible through its argument and not other static duration storage. The function may, however, visibly\nmodify the storage that it allocates. Calls to [A72][I73]aligned_alloc[/I73]()[/A72], [A74][I75]calloc[/I75]()[/A74], [A76][I77]free[/I77]()[/A76], [A78][I79]malloc[/I79]()[/A78], [S80][[A81]ADV[/A81]][/S80] [IMG82] &nbsp;[A83][I84]posix_memalign[/I84]()[/A83], [IMG85]\n\n[S86][[A87]CX[/A87]][/S86] [IMG88]\n[I89]reallocarray[/I89](), [IMG90] &nbsp;and [I91]realloc[/I91]() that allocate or\ndeallocate a particular region of memory shall occur in a single total order (see [A92][I93]4.15.1 Memory Ordering[/I93][/A92]), and each such deallocation call shall synchronize\nwith the next allocation (if any) in this order.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I66": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
