    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     41,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The ISO&nbsp;C standard makes it implementation-defined whether a call to [I172]realloc[/I172]([I173]p[/I173], 0) frees the space pointed to\nby [I174]p[/I174] if it returns a null pointer because memory for the new object was not allocated. POSIX.1 instead requires that\nimplementations set [I175]errno[/I175] if a null pointer is returned and the space has not been freed, and POSIX applications should only\nfree the space if [I176]errno[/I176] was changed.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I172": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
